; bfsodium SHA_512 ROUND : one round of the compression function
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The rotate  the exclusive or  the and and the adder
; are each PASTED from their own verified files; what is here is the wiring
; that FIPS 180_4 section 6 point 4 point 2 lays down and nothing else;
;
; INTERFACE entry=79 exit=0 footprint=0:276
; IO  in:  v{8} LE  Wt{8} LE  Kt{8} LE      (80 bytes)
;     out: v{8} LE                          (64 bytes)
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x00:0x3f  v{8}   u64 LE  a b c d e f g h  in and out
;   @0x40:0x47  Wt{8}  u64 LE  this round's schedule word; SPENT
;   @0x48:0x4f  Kt{8}  u64 LE  this round's constant; SPENT
;   @0x50:0x57  T1{8}  u64 LE
;   @0x58:0x5f  T2{8}  u64 LE
;   @0x60:0x67  s1{8}  u64 LE  scratch
;   @0x68:0x6f  s2{8}  u64 LE  scratch
;   @0x70:0x77  s3{8}  u64 LE  scratch
;   @0x78:0x7f  s4{8}  u64 LE  scratch
;   @0x80:0x87  s5{8}  u64 LE  scratch
;   @0x88:0x8f  tmp{8} u64 LE  the copy a read hands back
;   @0x90:0xab  the adder frame; add64 footprint 0:27 at @0x90
;   @0xb0:0xd5  the exclusive or frame; xor64 0:37 at @0xb0
;   @0xd8:0xfd  the and frame; and64 0:37 at @0xd8
;   @0x100:0x114  the rotate frame; rotr64 0:20 at @0x100
;
; The round is
;   T1 = h plus Sigma1(e) plus Ch(e f g) plus Kt plus Wt
;   T2 = Sigma0(a) plus Maj(a b c)
;   h g f e d c b a  becomes  g f e (d plus T1) c b a (T1 plus T2)
; and that last line is a CONVEYOR: the whole array shifts one word down and
; then two words are written; no variable is ever addressed by name;
;
; Ch is written  g xor (e and (f xor g))  and Maj  (a and b) xor (a and c) xor
; (b and c)  so between and64 and xor64 there is no need for a NOT;
;
; THE SAME SHAPE AS sha256/round  step for step; The two differ in the width
; of a word  in the six big sigma counts  and in nothing else: SHA_512 uses
; Sigma0 = ROTR 28 xor ROTR 34 xor ROTR 39 and Sigma1 = ROTR 14 xor ROTR 18
; xor ROTR 41  where SHA_256 uses 2 13 22 and 6 11 25; Read the two together;
;
; THE DISTANCES  worked out from the map above; A working variable is read by
; a THREE WAY COPY that drops it in a frame and in tmp at once  and tmp then
; hands the original straight back  because the round needs a b c e f g and h
; again after it has read them;
;   e @0x20 to the rotate frame @0x100 is 224  and tmp @0x88 sits 120 below it
;   a @0x00 to the rotate frame is 256  and tmp sits 136 above a
;   the rotate frame down to s1 @0x60 is 160  to s2 @0x68 is 152  to s3 @0x70
;     is 144
;   s1 and s2 up to the xor frame @0xb0 are both 80  and up to the and frame
;     @0xd8 are 120 and 112
;   the xor result @0xc0 comes down to s2 by 88  to s3 by 80 and to s4 by 72
;   the and result @0xe8 comes down to s2 by 128  to s4 by 112 and to s5 by 104
;
; A STEP RIGHT SHARES THE LINE WITH THE MOVE IT FOLLOWS  for the reason
; sha512/expand gives: eight bytes written the way sha256/round writes four is
; fifteen consecutive code lines with no annotation and bfstyle rule 4 refuses
; thirteen; it is also what keeps this file inside the size budget;

; read a b c d e f g h  then Wt  then Kt
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=79
; ASSERT zero 80:276

